n</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name><name><surname>Roth</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>B&#x000e9;trisey</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Marzo</surname><given-names>N</given-names></name><name><surname>Busato</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Offre et recours aux soins m&#x000e9;dicaux ambulatoires en Suisse</article-title><source>Volume Document de travail 22</source><year>2007</year><publisher-name>Neuchatel Switzerland: Schweizerisches Gesundheitsobservatorium</publisher-name><ext-link ext-link-type="uri" xlink:href="http://www.obsan.admin.ch/bfs/obsan/fr/index/05/publikationsdatenbank.Document.110590.pdf"/></citation></ref><ref id="B9"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Busato</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Kuenzi</surname><given-names>B</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Primary care physician supply and other key determinants of health care utilisation: The case of Switzerland</article-title><source>BMC Health Serv Res</source><year>2008</year><volume>8</volume><fpage>8</fpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">18190705</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1186/1472-6963-8-8</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B10"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Goodman</surname><given-names>DC</given-names></name><name><surname>Mick</surname><given-names>SS</given-names></name><name><surname>Bott</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name><name><surname>Stukel</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name><name><surname>Chang</surname><given-names>CH</given-names></name><name><surname>Marth</surname><given-names>N</given-names></name><name><surname>Poage</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Carretta</surname><given-names>HJ</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Primary care service areas: a new tool for the evaluation of primary care services</article-title><source>Health Serv Res</source><year>2003</year><volume>38</volume><fpage>287</fpage><lpage>309</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12650392</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1111/1475-6773.00116</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B11"><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Singer</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Willett</surname><given-names>JB</given-names></name></person-group><source>Applied longitudinal analysis</source><year>2003</year><publisher-name>New York: Oxford University Press</publisher-name></citation></ref><ref id="B12"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Singer</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Using SAS PROC MIXED to fit multilevel models, hierarchical models, and individual growth models</article-title><source>Journal of Educational and Behavioral Statistics</source><year>1998</year><volume>24</volume><fpage>323</fpage><lpage>355</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="B13"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Klauss</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name><name><surname>Staub</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name><name><surname>Widmer</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Busato</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Hospital service areas &#x02013; a new tool for health care planning in Switzerland</article-title><source>BMC Health Serv Res</source><year>2005</year><volume>5</volume><fpage>33</fpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15882463</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1186/1472-6963-5-33</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B14"><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Bisig</surname><given-names>B</given-names></name><name><surname>Gutzwiler</surname><given-names>F</given-names></name></person-group><source>Gesundheitswesen Schweiz: Gibt es Unter- oder &#x000dc;berversorgung? Band 2: Detailresultate</source><year>2004</year><volume>2</volume><publisher-name>Verlag Ruegger Z&#x000fc;rich/Chur</publisher-name></citation></ref><ref id="B15"><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Bisig</surname><given-names>B</given-names></name><name><surname>Gutzwiler</surname><given-names>F</given-names></name></person-group><source>Gesundheitswesen Schweiz: Gibt es Unter- oder &#x000dc;berversorgung? Band 1: Gesamt&#x000fc;bersicht</source><year>2004</year><volume>2</volume><publisher-name>Verlag Ruegger Z&#x000fc;rich/Chur</publisher-name></citation></ref><ref id="B16"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Crivelli</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name><name><surname>Filippini</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Mosca</surname><given-names>I</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Federalism and regional health care expenditures: an empirical analysis for the Swiss cantons</article-title><source>Health Econ</source><year>2006</year><volume>15</volume><fpage>535</fpage><lpage>541</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16389663</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1002/hec.1072</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B17"><citation citation-type="other"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Nocera</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Wanzenried</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>On the Dynamics of Physician Density; Theory and Empirical Evidence for Switzerland</article-title><source>Research Papers in Economics</source><year>2002</year><ext-link ext-link-type="uri" xlink:href="http://ideas.repec.org/p/ube/dpvwib/dp0208.html"/></citation></ref><ref id="B18"><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><su